# Secrets — never commit. The API key, the Metabase login and warehouse credentials
# live in .env only. `.env*` also catches .envrc (direnv) and .env-prod; the one
# tracked exception is the placeholder template, un-ignored by the `!` line below.
.env*
!.env.example
*.pem
credentials*

# Data — publish aggregates and code, never the raw corpus (PROJECT_BRIEF §2.5).
# data/snapshots/ (the weekly public aggregates, Phase 4), data/damir/ (the
# tracked, numbers-only claim-cost fit, Phase 7b) and data/ameli/ (the tracked,
# numbers-only fee split, Phase 9i) are the tracked subtrees; `data/*` (not
# `data/`) is what lets the negations below work. The raw fetched DAMIR month
# under data/cache/damir/ and the hand-downloaded data.ameli export under
# data/cache/ameli/ stay ignored (never committed).
data/*
!data/snapshots/
!data/damir/
!data/ameli/
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal

# Claude Code config is local-only: a tracked settings/.mcp.json would auto-run
# an inbound branch's hooks or MCP servers for anyone opening the repo
# (CLAUDE.md → Project tooling). Agent, command and skill prose and hook
# scripts ARE tracked.
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
.mcp.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/scheduled_tasks.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
